<bioghist encodinganalog="545$a">
<head>Biographical Information
</head>
<p>William Tisinger was born 1 September 1816 in Shenandoah County, Virginia, to John Tisinger (1777-1854) and Elizabeth Catherine Bowman Tisinger (1776-1842).  William Tisinger became surveyor for Shenandoah County.  He married Amelia H. Will (1820-1885) 14 June 1848, and they had six children.  Their son Joseph Homer Tisinger (1853-1938) was a farmer.  He married Julia Arnetta Henkel (1859-1911) and they had seven children.
</p>
<p>Reuben Bird Will (1830-1913) was the brother of Amelia Will Tisinger, and they were the children of George Will.  Sallie Elizabeth Will (1856-1912) was the daughter of their sister, Mary Will.
</p>
<p>Siram Peter Henkel (1809-1879) was the father of Julia Arnetta Henkel Tisinger.  Lewis P. Henkel (1837-1904) was her brother.  Solomon D. Henkel (1815-1872) was Julia Tisinger's and Lewis Henkel's uncle, and Siram Henkel's brother.
</p>
</bioghist>
<scopecontent encodinganalog="520$a">
<head>Scope and Content
</head>
<p>Papers, 1823-1918, of the Tisinger family of Shenandoah County, Virginia, consisting of accounts, correspondence, court records, deeds, estate records, receipts, and other documents of the Tisinger family, including William Tisinger (1816-1887), surveyor of Shenandoah County.  Papers include accounts, correspondence, estate records, and other documents of the Henkel and Will families of Shenandoah County.
</p>
</scopecontent>
